    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the GOLD membership tier for owners whose household reaches 3+ members after a create, following the codebase's existing \"compute a snapshot at create, derive the tier at read\" pattern (mirroring `namesakeCount`).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`OwnerMapper.membershipTier(...)`** \u2014 returns `GOLD` when the owner's stored `householdSize >= 3`; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules apply unchanged. GOLD takes priority.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (so the generated `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` includes it) and updated the description.\n\n3. **`AssignHouseholdSize`** (new OfficeFloor function) \u2014 after `AssignHouseholdId` and before `SaveOwner`, it counts owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` plus the owner itself (1 when there's no household), storing the snapshot on the entity. Wired into `owners.POST.yml`.\n\n4. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 new persisted `household_size` field, plus the `household_size INTEGER` column added to all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)`** \u2014 ignores the new `householdSize` target, consistent with how `householdId`/`namesakeCount` are handled.\n\nThe snapshot semantics match the spec's wording (\"has 3 or more members **after this create**\"): the third member of a shared household is created with `householdSize = 3` and reads back as `GOLD`.",
